&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;At Relativity Space, we’re building rockets to serve today’s needs and tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Our&amp;nbsp;Terran R vehicle will deliver customer payloads to orbit, meeting the growing demand for launch&amp;nbsp;capacity. But that’s just the start. Achieving commercial success with Terran R will unlock new&amp;nbsp;opportunities to advance science, exploration, and innovation, pioneering progress that reaches beyond&amp;nbsp;the known.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;Joining Relativity means becoming part of something where autonomy, ownership, and impact exist at every level. Here, you&#39;re not just executing tasks; you&#39;re solving problems that haven’t been solved before, helping develop a rocket, a factory, and a business from the ground up. Whether you’re in propulsion, manufacturing, software, avionics, or a corporate function, you’ll collaborate across teams, shape decisions, and see your work come to life in record time. Relativity is a place where creativity and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;technical rigor go hand in hand, and your voice will help define the stories we’re writing together. Now&amp;nbsp;is a unique moment in time where it’s early enough to leave your mark on the product, the process, and&amp;nbsp;the culture, but far enough along that Terran R is tangible and picking up momentum. The most&amp;nbsp;meaningful work of your career is waiting. Join us.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environmental Test Lab: Vibration Test Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Vibration Test Team provides vibration testing services across the Terran R program, supporting hardware and systems for Avionics, Propulsion, and Mechanisms. The team partners closely with engineering organizations to execute environmental testing that validates hardware performance and readiness throughout development and qualification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a second-shift position with a standard schedule of Monday through Friday, 3:00 p.m. to 1:30 a.m. PT. The role is structured around a 50-hour workweek, including 10 guaranteed overtime hours each week. In addition to base pay, employees receive a 10% shift differential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Environmental Test Specialist focused on vibration testing, you will execute acceptance, qualification, and development testing on Terran R hardware. This role requires strong hands-on knowledge of electromechanical shaker systems, instrumentation, test setup, and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and execute vibration acceptance, qualification, and development tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate electromechanical shaker systems and understand the function and interaction of their major components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot vibration test setups, including control issues, instrumentation problems, and fixture-related concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, configure, and validate accelerometers and other test instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand vibration control systems and identify abnormal test or system behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering teams to communicate test status, troubleshoot issues, and support successful test execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work safely around high-voltage systems, high-pressure systems, and cryogenic environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly document and communicate test configurations, observations, issues, and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on vibration testing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of vibration control systems and vibration test equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency with accelerometers, instrumentation, data acquisition, and measurement equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot vibration test setups, control problems, instrumentation, and test fixtures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of electrical theory and electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of thermal principles and their impact on hardware and test environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong computer skills and ability to work with test control, data acquisition, and technical software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical communication and documentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working hands-on with complex test hardware in a dynamic test environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical or vocational training is preferred. Aerospace, defense, or other high-reliability hardware testing experience is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional environmental or dynamics testing experience in one or more of the following areas is a plus:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical shock testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acceleration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acoustic testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environmental qualification testing of aerospace or flight hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test fixture setup, evaluation, or troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting development, qualification, and acceptance test campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
